bevy-horizon: flatten small ifs before Volta (NAK_DEBUG=psel)

For mesa-switch (https://github.com/danfromtico/mesa-switch, by danfromtico and NaGaa95; MIT)
at 953fa75a, after 0001-0025. scripts/build_nvk.sh applies it; this text before the first
"diff --git" line is ignored by git apply.

Before SM70 every if NAK keeps is a real branch, with SSY, BRA and SYNC around it, and NAK ran
nir_opt_peephole_select with a limit of 0, so it only flattened empty ifs. With psel, an if
whose sides hold up to 8 instructions becomes selects. Switch builds turn psel on with the other
defaults (patch 0019); NAK_DEBUG=-psel turns it off. The flags key NVK's shader cache, so
shaders compiled with and without it are cached apart. Not yet timed with Skate 3 (sk8 findings
61).

The change is StevensND's (https://github.com/StevensND), from his Mesa patch for the reference
Switch port of the ReXGlue recompilation framework, as carried by masseffect-nx's NVK patch
(https://github.com/nebadasSwifty/masseffect-nx, mesa/mesa-switch-masseffect.patch, by
nebadasSwifty; MIT, as its THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md puts its mesa/ changes).

